# ParchLock local repository.
#
# Everything here is grounded in the project's own build scripts rather than a
# generic template: build-android.bat states outright that "Release signing
# material must remain outside this repository", and it regenerates
# capacitor-www and android/app/src/main/assets/public on every run.
# make-dist.bat's source-archive allow-list names the same exclusions --
# "Never include games, AI/internal docs, build output, generated Android
# assets, secrets or signing material".
#
# One deliberate difference: the AI/internal docs, harness and tools ARE
# tracked here. make-dist excludes them from the archive shipped to users for
# licence-compliance reasons; for version control they are the project's own
# decision log and test suites, which is exactly what history should hold.

# ---- dependencies -----------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---- generated by build-android.bat -----------------------------------
# make-dist.bat writes this whole tree, then `cap copy` mirrors it.
capacitor-www/
# Wiped with rmdir /s /q and rebuilt on every Android build.
android/app/src/main/assets/*
# capacitor.plugins.json is the plugin registry that `cap update`/`cap sync` writes and
# `cap copy` (the only cap step build-android.bat runs) does not. It is tracked so a clean
# checkout or worktree still ships TextToSpeech/SpeechRecognition (APK regression 2026-10-31).
!android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json
ParchLock-source.zip
ParchLock.exe

# ---- Gradle / Android build output -------------------------------------
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/captures/
.gradle/

# ---- secrets and machine-specific paths --------------------------------
# build-android.bat: "Release signing material must remain outside this
# repository" -- it takes the keystore from PARCHLOCK_KEYSTORE et al, never
# from a tracked file. local.properties holds this machine's SDK path.
android/local.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.apk
.env
.env.*

# ---- large test captures ------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable by re-running the suites; ~22MB of PNGs otherwise.
tools/screenshots/
harness/screenshots/
harness/shots-*/
# tools/anchorhead-regression.js writes this one to the repo root on every run
# (line 76, `path: 'anchorhead-after-fix.png'`), so it is regenerated output
# rather than debris -- ignored so a test run never leaves the tree dirty.
anchorhead-after-fix.png

# ---- bus runtime state --------------------------------------------------
# .ai-bus/bin and the config are tracked; the runtime directory is live
# per-session state (~22MB), not source.
.ai-bus/runtime/

# ---- story files --------------------------------------------------------
# 309 third-party story files, ~127MB. make-dist.bat deliberately keeps these
# out of the distributed source archive ("Never include games ... Rights review
# and removal before release are the operator's manual responsibility", D97).
# Excluded here too so the repository stays a manageable size. If you would
# rather have them versioned, delete the next line -- nothing else depends on
# this choice.
games/

# ---- user data ----------------------------------------------------------
user/*
!user/_user-files-go-here.txt

# ---- editor / OS noise --------------------------------------------------
*.log
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- local scratch and runtime data (D215 cleanup, claude/codex consensus) ----
# Kept on disk, never versioned: scratch from both seats, status-audit dumps,
# Glulx runtime data written beside the launcher, and native hook build output.
/tmp/
/work/status-audit/
/shot.png
/*.glkdata
/native-hooks/build/
# Future scratch probes stay local; tracked probes cited as evidence are unaffected.
harness/_*.js
harness/_*.json
harness/_*.txt

# E6 (grok audit work/investigations/e6-audit/AUDIT-grok.md, claude apply 11-07): copied runtime
# trees from gate runs and gate stream shards are reproducible; their reports stay tracked.
/work/mapping-research/items-codex/resume-20261020/review-20261025/z3p178/base/
/work/mapping-research/items-codex/resume-20261020/review-20261025/z3p178/cand/
